      "textEn": "119\n\nEnjoys. Similarly, the patient dies even after all the treatment. In this physical world, where\nthe struggle for life is ongoing, people have discovered many means of protection, but if God\ncondemns them, they become in vain. Therefore, the gods deliberately said—Truthful, you\nWe surrender.—O Lord! You alone are the protector; therefore, we take refuge in you. God wants people to come to his refuge (Sarvadharman parityajya mamekam sharanam vraja) and\nHe further says—\n\nSakrudeva pranapanno yastavasti iti chachate. May I, the abode of fearlessness, be the giver of all this. “If someone sincerely comes to my refuge saying, 'Oh Lord! From today, I am in your refuge.\nSo I always provide him with protection. It's my fast.” (Ramayana, Book 18, Chapter 33). The gods praised God because to protect all the devotees who were being tormented by Kansa and his associates,\nGod had now appeared in the womb of his devotee Devaki.\nIn this way, God\nplays the role of Satyavrata. The protection provided by God cannot be compared to the protection given by the gods. It is said that Ravana was a great devotee of Shiva, but when\nLord Ramchandra went to kill him, Shiva could not provide him protection. Brahmaji and Shiva, along with great sages like Narad and many other gods, came to Kansa's house\ndisappearing. They began to praise God with such selected verses that are dear to the devotees and\nfulfill desires. In the initial words, he has said that God is firm in his vow. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, Krishna incarnates in this material world only to protect the virtuous and destroy the wicked. It is her fast. The gods understood that\nGod has already resided in Devaki's womb to fulfill this vow of his.\nThey were very pleased\nthat God is appearing to fulfill his purpose, and they addressed him by saying Satyam Param. Every person is in search of the truth. That is the philosophical style of life. The deity gives this information"
