      "textEn": "129\n\nIs equal. His goal is Param Padam, meaning Vaikuntha, where there is neither physical suffering nor at every step\nthere is danger. (Bhagavata .14.58) Brahmaji and great men like Shiva (Swayambhurnaradah: Shambhu:) have prescribed this\nmethod, therefore, to overcome ignorance, we should adopt this method. This\nis extremely simple, but we should follow the footsteps of the great people, only then can we achieve success.\nCan achieve. Regarding the word 'Mahatkruten', it is also an important point that the method shown by great devotees\nis not only for them but also for others. Those who simplify things in this way\nIt not only makes it easier for them but also for those who follow them. In this verse,\nthe method that has been described to cross the ocean of ignorance is not only for a devotee but\nalso for any common person who follows a devotee (Mahajano yane gatah sa pathah). Self-exalted, exceedingly difficult, radiant, blazing,\nThe ocean of existence, the mighty, the intoxicated, the cloud-like, and the friend.\nYou are the abode of the lotus-like feet of the world.\nYou are the one who bestows grace. 31. Meaning of the word\n\nSwayam—self, you; Samuttiriya—crossing; Su-durantaram—difficult; Dyumna—like the sun in the darkness of this world of ignorance;\nChamakanwale he Prabhu; Bhav-Arnavam—ocean of world; Bhimam—terrible; Adabhra-saohrudaah—devotees who are towards the fallen souls;\nBhavat-pad-ambhuruh—your lotus feet; Navam—to cross; Atra—in this world; Te—they (Vaishnavas); Nidhayah—leaving behind; Yataah—the ultimate goal, Vaikuntha; Sat-anugrahaah—always merciful and kind to devotees; Bhavan—you. Oh, radiant Lord, you are always ready to fulfill the desires of your devotees, that is why\nyou are called the wish-fulfilling tree. When the teachers, out of fear of ignorance, to cross the terrible ocean of existence,\ntake refuge in your lotus feet, then they leave behind their method\nby which they cross over. Because you are very kind to your other devotees, therefore,\nyou accept this method to help them.\nMeaning: This statement reveals how kind teachers and compassionate God\ncome together to help that serious devotee who wants to return to the abode of God. Shri chaitanya"
